    board(pm): record the measured publish workaround on CF-190 — SSH is intermittent, HTTPS+gh token is deterministic
    
    CF-190 was filed from one lane's failed push. Measured on the same host minutes
    later, the SSH path is intermittent rather than dead: 'ssh -T git@github.com'
    authenticated once, then refused four consecutive times with
    'Permission denied (publickey)', then succeeded again. Every candidate key under
    ~/.ssh was refused while failing (id_ed25519, id_rsa, id_ed25519_npu,
    id_ed25519_nas, id_ed25519_m10, id_ed25519_bunker, hermes-hetzner) and
    'ssh-add -l' reports 'The agent has no identities', so no loaded identity
    explains the successes.
    
    The publish path that does resolve deterministically: gh holds a repo-scoped
    token, so
      GIT_ASKPASS=<helper running 'gh auth token'> GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 \
        git push https://github.com/coding-hermes/code-factory.git main
    prints 'Everything up-to-date' and
      git ls-remote https://github.com/coding-hermes/code-factory.git refs/heads/main
    returns the local HEAD hash (730fee9 at write time). The token never appears on
    a command line: the helper execs 'gh auth token' at runtime.
    
    The note on the row states the decidable remedy (fall back to that path and
    record which path each push used) so the row can be closed with a check rather
    than a retry habit.
    
