 {"id": "CF-188", "title": "P4 — the README lane census paragraph quotes `code-factory-duckbrain admission=tasks` for 2026-11-04, and its own recipe now prints `admission=cooldown`", "status": "pending", "priority": "P4", "complexity": 1, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-04 by the code-factory-duckbrain-dogfood tick code-factory-duckbrain-dogfood-2026-11-04-08-40-09 (third execution) from a clean clone of origin/main at d65adf9: the census recipe README.md ships in 'The lanes' was run verbatim (the `BLOCK`/`jq` subshell at README.md:162-199 run against http://127.0.0.1:9090) and printed 19 rows: 13 of the 14 shipped lanes enabled=true, `code-factory-qa enabled=false`, all 13 satellites `parent=code-factory`, and `code-factory-duckbrain admission=cooldown`. Every number in the paragraph reproduces except its last sentence: README.md:215-216 asserts 'The same run printed `code-factory-duckbrain admission=tasks` against the `cooldown` the loader writes — the drift the command exists to expose.' The same run today prints `admission=cooldown`, i.e. no drift, so the sentence states the opposite of what the command it ships measures. CF-058 (complete) closed the original admission contradiction by rewriting this paragraph around the live reading, and the paragraph is dated ('On the reference deployment, on 2026-11-04') and written in the present tense, so a reader who runs the recipe gets a contradiction of the document that taught them to run it. The class is the one CF-155/CF-186 police in the section census: a hand-written live-state claim with no tip or timestamp binding it to the run that measured it.", "acceptance_criteria": "0. Reproduce from the repo root: the census block copied out of README.md 'The lanes' prints `19` then a lane list whose `code-factory-duckbrain` row reads `admission=cooldown`, while README.md:215-216 claims the same run printed `admission=tasks`.\n1. The paragraph agrees with a re-run of the command it ships: it either states the currently measu